@host = http://localhost:5000

### The whole system, with nothing of Module 1 left in it
GET {{host}}/api/events/1/availability

### The vertical slice — one file, straight to EF
GET {{host}}/api/schedule

### Buy ten -> the aggregate applies the 10% bulk discount
### 10 x 49.99 = 499.90, minus 10% = 449.91
POST {{host}}/api/events/1/purchases
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 10, "customerEmail": "reader@example.com" }

### --- Purchase: the full stack, end to end ---

### Buy two tickets
POST {{host}}/api/events/1/purchases
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 2, "customerEmail": "reader@example.com" }

### A declined card -> 409, and NOTHING committed: no reservation, no domain events
POST {{host}}/api/events/1/purchases
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 2, "customerEmail": "decline@example.com" }

### Refund one ticket — capacity returns and the money goes back
### (paste in the paymentReference the purchase above gave you)
POST {{host}}/api/events/1/refunds
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 1, "paymentReference": "CH-a1b2c3d4..." }

### --- Minimal API endpoints (the clean controllers are gone) ---

### Available events (was /api/catalog/available-events before Module 7)
GET {{host}}/api/events/available

### Availability — now a sub-resource of the event
GET {{host}}/api/events/1/availability

### Reserve three tickets
POST {{host}}/api/events/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 3 }

### Invalid quantity -> 400 from the validation behavior
POST {{host}}/api/events/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 0 }

### Unknown event -> 404 ProblemDetails, no exception thrown
POST {{host}}/api/events/999/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 1 }

### Oversell -> 409 ProblemDetails, no exception thrown
POST {{host}}/api/events/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 100000 }
